<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70630" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νη-έω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾱέω</span></b> , older form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέω</span> (c), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>heap, pile up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ αὐτῶν νήησαν ξύλα πολλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.64
				</span></i>
			; of a funeral pile, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μενοεικέα νήεον ὕλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.139
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ δὲ δρατᾲ σώματα
			νήει</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				169
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ τ᾽ εὖ νηῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.322
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀπήνης νήεον . .
				ἀπερείσι᾽ ἄποινα</span>
			<i>heaped</i> a huge ransom, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.276
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήεον αὐτόθι βωμόν</span>
			<i>piled</i> it <i>up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.403
			</span></i>:—in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὰν ναήσατ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					3.33
				</span></i>
			: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηήσεται</span> in pass. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.216
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pile, load,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηήσας εὖ νῆας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.358
				</span></i>
			:—in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα ἅλις</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῦ—νηησάσθω</span>
			<i>let him pile his</i> ship with gold enough, ib.<i><span class="en">
				137
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				279
			</span></i>. [Sts. corrupted to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηνέω,</span>
			q.v.]</div>
